---
/** 2026-10-01 cleanup round, item 2: rewritten so the sources list and the
 *  "how often" line are GENERATED from the actual per-town config
 *  (via lib/about-sources.ts's aboutSourcesFor(), the same "can't drift"
 *  machinery /about already uses) instead of a Brookings-only hand-written
 *  table with every other town falling back to a vague blurb -- the
 *  previous version leaked Brookings-shaped assumptions ("every hour")
 *  onto Moreno Valley and Broomfield, which don't share that cadence, and
 *  never enumerated Ticketmaster, Chamber/GrowthZone, or Worker Pulse's own
 *  sourcing at all.
 *
 *  Three facts below were explicitly verified against the real pipeline
 *  before writing this page, not assumed:
 *   1. No person reviews an item before it appears. Checked:
 *      ai_pipeline/publish.py's only "human review" reference (line ~699)
 *      is queuing an unresolved VENUE NAME STRING for a data-quality
 *      review queue (ai_pipeline/venue_registry.py) -- unrelated to content
 *      approval. There is no gate between generation and publish anywhere
 *      in the pipeline.
 *   2. The real cadence is twice a day (11:00 and 23:00 UTC, the cron-dispatcher
 *      Worker's "0 11,23 * * *"); weather is fetched every hour by the same Worker.
 *      Text rewritten 2026-11-06 (owner-approved proposal): no model-written text is
 *      shown anywhere, so the old "language model" / "AI summaries" sections are gone.
 *   3. /corrections exists, links from /contact, and honestly shows "No
 *      corrections have been logged yet" rather than being an empty stub.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../lib/site-config';
import { metaDescription } from '../lib/meta-description';
import { forCountry } from '../lib/country-profile';
import { aboutSourcesFor } from '../lib/about-sources';

const sources = aboutSourcesFor(siteConfig.townId);
---
<BaseLayout title={`How we gather this — ${siteConfig.siteName}`}
  description={metaDescription('how-we-gather', siteConfig)}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>How we gather this</h1>
    <p>{siteConfig.siteName} doesn't have a newsroom. It collects public
    information from the sources listed below, checks them twice a day, and
    shows what they publish: dates, times, places, agenda items, notices and
    links. We don't write news stories, and no model-written text is shown on
    the site. No person reviews an item before it appears; the checks
    described below run automatically.</p>

    <h2>The sources</h2>
    {sources.length > 0 ? (
      <ul class="sources">
        {sources.map((s) => (
          <li><a href={s.url} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{s.name}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    ) : (
      <p>{siteConfig.sourceBlurb}</p>
    )}
    <p>This list is generated from the same configuration the collectors
    run from. If a source is switched off, it drops off this page on the next
    build.</p>

    <h2>How often</h2>
    <p>Event calendars, meeting agendas, school and public notices are
    collected twice a day. Weather is updated every hour. Each page says when
    it was last updated. A change at the source can take up to half a day to
    show here; for anything time-critical, use the link to the source.</p>

    <h2>What we show</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Meetings:</strong> the date, time and place, the agenda item
      titles exactly as the agenda gives them, and links to the agenda, minutes
      and video. A meeting is marked Cancelled or Postponed only when the
      source itself says so in a status or notice field.</li>
      <li><strong>Events:</strong> the title, date, time and venue as the
      {forCountry(siteConfig.country, 'organizer', 'organiser')} published them, with a link back to the organiser. "Free" and
      age labels appear only when the source states them.</li>
      <li><strong>Weather and alerts:</strong> forecasts and warnings from {siteConfig.country === 'gb' ? 'the Met Office' : 'the National Weather Service'}, shown as published.</li>
      <li><strong>Traffic, school closures and public notices:</strong> the
      notices as the road authority or the school district posts them, with a
      link.</li>
      {siteConfig.bigShows?.enabled && (
        <li><strong>Big shows nearby:</strong> concerts, sports and touring shows
        from Ticketmaster at venues within {siteConfig.bigShows.maxMiles} miles. They are listed separately and are
        never counted as events in town. Prices are not shown, and distance is
        measured in a straight line from the town center (shown as "Denver · 13
        mi"), not as a driving distance.</li>
      )}
    </ul>

    <h2>What we work out ourselves</h2>
    <p>Software, not a model, converts times to {siteConfig.cityName}'s time
    zone, removes duplicates between sources, and sorts events into groups from
    the source's own category or from keywords in the title. Where a source gives
    no value, we show nothing rather than guess.</p>

    <h2>What we choose not to name</h2>
    <p>Meeting agendas sometimes include the names of private individuals —
    someone applying for a variance, say, or a permit. We refer to people by
    role instead ("an applicant for the variance") rather than by name.
    {forCountry(siteConfig.country, 'Organizations', 'Organisations')}, businesses, and public officials acting in their official
    capacity are named normally. We don't cover arrests, court records or
    obituaries.</p>

    <h2>Sources we do not read</h2>
    <p>If a source's robots.txt forbids automated reading, or it blocks us, we
    don't collect from it. We show a plain link to it instead, and never try to
    get around the block.</p>

    <h2>Photos</h2>
    <p>Illustrative photos on category and topic pages come from Pexels,
    each individually credited to its photographer where it appears. They
    represent the general subject, not a specific event pictured in the
    story next to them.{siteConfig.bigShows?.enabled && ' Ticketmaster images appear on its own listings.'}</p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>If something here is wrong, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> and
    we'll fix it — usually within one refresh cycle, since the site rebuilds
    automatically. Logged corrections are public: see the
    <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.prose { max-width: 40rem; }
.prose h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
.prose p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }

.sources { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: 0.375rem; }
.sources li { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
</style>
